- text: Hello, world! 07:43 PM · 10/7/2026 Real-time update from second client! 07:43 PM · 10/7/2026\n</tool_response><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nPage 2 shows both messages. Let me check page 1 to verify it received the real-time update via SSE:\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=browser_switch_page>\n<parameter=page>\npage-1\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\nSwitched to page-1.\nURL: http://localhost:5173/  TITLE: Message Board\nOPEN PAGES: page-1 (active) http://localhost:5173/ | page-2 http://localhost:5173/\nPAGE STRUCTURE:\n- heading \"📋 Message Board\" [level=1]\n- textbox \"Type a message...\"\n- button \"Send\"\n- text: Hello, world! 07:43 PM · 10/7/2026 Real-time update from second client! 07:43 PM · 10/7/2026\n</tool_response><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nBoth messages appear on page-1. The SSE real-time broadcast is working correctly - the message posted from page-2 was received by page-1 in real-time.\n\nLet me also verify the API endpoints directly:\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=run_command>\n<parameter=command>\ncurl -s http://localhost:3001/api/messages | head -c 500\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n$ curl -s http://localhost:3001/api/messages | head -c 500\n[exit 0]\nSTDOUT:\n[{\"id\":1,\"text\":\"Hello, world!\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-08T00:43:01.406Z\"},{\"id\":2,\"text\":\"Real-time update from second client!\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-08T00:43:07.822Z\"}]\n</tool_response><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=run_command>\n<parameter=command>\ncurl -s -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/messages -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"text\":\"API test message\"}' 2>&1\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/messages -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\